<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tây Sơn dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1778">1778</a>–<a href="/years/1802">1802</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Tây Sơn, Tay Son dynasty, Tay Son rebellion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tây Sơn were three brothers from Tây Sơn in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> who led a peasant rebellion from 1771. They destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyễn lords</a> in the south, defeated a Siamese invasion in 1785, overthrew the Trịnh lords in the north in 1786 and routed a Qing army in 1789 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quang-trung">Nguyễn Huệ</a> (Emperor Quang Trung). Divided after his death in 1792, they were destroyed in 1802 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-long">Nguyễn Ánh</a>, founder of the Nguyễn dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty.jpg" alt="Tây Sơn dynasty" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DannamEmpire · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vietnam_in_late_18th_century_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
